rdered pair (i, j) with i < j. If any valid pair exists that sums to target, this search space is guaranteed to find it.\",\r\n22:         \"commonMistakes\": [\r\n23:           \"Starting the inner loop at j = 0 or j = i instead of j = i + 1, which accidentally reuses the same element twice.\",\r\n24:           \"Time limit exceeded (TLE) on large arrays: n\\u00b2 operations exceed the execution limit when n = 10,000.\",\r\n25:           \"Returning values [nums[i], nums[j]] instead of indices [i, j].\"\r\n26:         ],\r\n27:         \"isVerified\": true\r\n28:       },\r\n29:       {\r\n30:         \"id\": \"optimized\",\r\n31:         \"name\": \"Approach 2: One-Pass Hash Map (Optimized)\",\r\n32:         \"isOptimal\": true,\r\n33:         \"timeComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n34:         \"spaceComplexity\": \"O(n)\",\r\n35:         \"code\": \"def twoSum(nums, target):\\n    prevMap = {}\\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\\n        diff = target - nums[i]\\n        if diff in prevMap:\\n            return [prevMap[diff], i]\\n        prevMap[nums[i]] = i\\n    return []\\n\\nnums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\\nprint(\\\"Indices:\\\", twoSum(nums, 9))\",\r\n36:         \"explanation\": \"Maintain a hash map mapping each seen number to its index. In a single pass, for each element nums[i], calculate the required complement diff = target - nums[i]. If diff exists in the map, return [prevMap[diff], i]. Otherwise, record nums[i] in the map.\",\r\n37:         \"whyItWorks\": \"As we iterate left to right, if a pair (a, b) sums to target, when we arrive at the second element b, element a is already stored in the hash map. Hash table lookups operate in O(1) average time, reducing the total search time to O(n).\",\r\n38:         \"commonMistakes\": [\r\n39:           \"Inserting nums[i] into the hash map BEFORE checking if diff is in prevMap, which erroneously matches an element with itself.\",\r\n40:           \"Overwriting earlier indices when duplicate numbers appear before the complement search occurs.\",\r\n41:           \"Assuming the input list is sorted and attempting two-pointer converging without sorting first.\"\r\n42:         ],\r\n43:         \"isVerified\": true\r\n44:       }\r\n45:     ]\r\n46:   },\r\n47:   \"2\": {\r\n48:     \"hasMultipleApproaches\": true,\r\n49:     \"approaches\": [\r\n50:       {\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
